  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Zone to zone – from 3v3 into a 2v1",
  "description": "The pitch is split into two zones: a press zone and a play zone, with a goal and a goalkeeper at each end. A 3v3 is played in the press zone, and one player from each team waits in the play zone. The drill starts on a signal with the ball at the attacking team in the press zone.\n\nThe attackers try to get into the play zone with the ball under control – either by dribbling in or by passing to the team-mate already there. Only one attacker may follow into the play zone, which makes it a 2v1. The defending team tries to win the ball in the press zone and score straight away. Play stops at a goal; on the coach's signal everyone resets and it starts again. Progression: the ball may only enter the play zone by dribbling.\n\nHow the pitch is split and where the goals are is an interpretation – adapt it to your hall. The drill is made for 10 players.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Show that you are available – with your voice, stick and body."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Position yourself so the ball carrier has a forward pass in depth."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Time your run: move when the ball carrier can pass, not too early."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Aim the pass in front of your team-mate so they can take it at speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp5",
      "text": "In the play zone: use the 2v1 – draw the defender and pass on."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
